00:34:10,069 --> 00:34:23,341
我断言你可以做 3 次旋转：旋转 120 度、它的平方（240度）或它的立方（单位元），这些旋转都保持正四面体。
And I claim you can do three rotations: you can rotate by 120 degrees, or you could do its square, or its cube, and those preserve the tetrahedron.

133
00:34:23,341 --> 00:34:35,360
因此绕这条轴有 3 个保持正四面体的旋转。
So there are three rotations around this axis preserving the tetrahedron.

134
00:34:35,536 --> 00:34:47,062
好的，同理，对于任意其他顶点，绕穿过该顶点并垂直于对面的轴也有 3 个旋转。这个顶点并无任何特殊之处：如果我从这个顶点开始，
Okay, likewise, for any other vertex there are three rotations around the axis that goes through the vertex and is perpendicular So there was nothing special about this vertex: if I started with this vertex,

135
00:34:47,062 --> 00:35:11,160
取穿过该顶点与对侧中心相连的轴，绕该轴旋转正四面体，我依然有 3 个保持正四面体的旋转。特别地，无论 S_4 的这个子群是什么，它在顶点集合 S 上传递作用。
and I took the axis through the vertex and the midpoint of that side, and I rotated the tetrahedron around that axis, I'd still have three rotations that preserve the tetrahedron. Okay, in particular, whatever this subgroup of S_4 is, it acts transitively on the set S of vertices.

136
00:35:11,160 --> 00:35:27,782
因为仅取绕穿过此处的轴的 3 个旋转，就能传递地置换另外 3 个顶点；如果我想证明这三个顶点与该顶点处于同一个轨道，我取绕另一条轴的旋转，它能传递地置换那些顶点。
Because just taking the three rotations around the axis going through here permutes these three vertices transitively; and if I want to show that these three vertices are in the same orbit as this vertex, I take a rotation around this other axis, and that permutes those vertices transitively.

137
00:35:27,782 --> 00:35:35,402
所以我可以借助该群中的某个元素从任意顶点到达任意另一个顶点。好的，所以这是一个传递作用。
So I can get from any vertex to any other vertex with some element in this group. Okay, so that's a transitive action.

138
00:35:35,402 --> 00:35:47,510
因此 4 必定等于G 的阶除以固定某个顶点的稳定子群的阶。
So therefore 4 has to be equal to the order of G divided by the order of G stabilizing a vertex.

139
00:35:47,510 --> 00:36:02,299
因为这是 S 的大小，它是一个单一轨道，所以必须等于群的阶除以固定顶点的稳定子群的阶。但固定顶点的稳定子群的阶显然是 3，对吧？
That's because this is the size of S, it's a single orbit, so that has to be the order of the group divided by the order of the group stabilizing a vertex. But the order of the group stabilizing a vertex is clearly 3, right?

140
00:36:02,299 --> 00:36:10,480
因为它必须置换另外这三个顶点；如果我再固定其中一个，旋转就是平凡的了。
Because it has to permute these three vertices around; if I fixed one of them, then the rotation is trivial.

141
00:36:10,480 --> 00:36:17,340
所以仅有的可能就是旋转 120 度或旋转 240 度，因此这是一个 3 阶子群。
So the only possibilities are a rotation through 120 degrees or a rotation through 240 degrees, so that's a group of order 3.

142
00:36:17,340 --> 00:36:30,495
于是我们得到 4 等于 G 的阶除以 3，由计数公式可知 G 的阶是 12，且它是 S_4（阶数为 24）的一个子群。
So we get 4 is the order of G divided by 3, and that tells us from the counting formula that the order of G is 12, and it's a subgroup of this group S_4, which has order 24.

143
00:36:30,495 --> 00:36:48,590
事实证明——虽然我们还没证明，但可以证明 S_4 只有唯一一个阶数为12 的子群，那就是——你们知道一个，所以不妨告诉我，如果我说只有一个，它是谁？正是 A_4！
Now it turns out—we haven't proved it yet, but it turns out there's only one subgroup of S_4 which has order 12, and that is—you know one, so why not tell me, if I tell you there's only one, what is it? A_4, exactly!

144
00:36:55,000 --> 00:37:01,320
S_4 唯一一个 12 阶子群。
The only subgroup of S_4 of order 12.

145
00:37:01,320 --> 00:37:31,436
我们还没证明这点，不过如果你思考它如何置换顶点以及我们在这个群中得到了哪些可能的元素，这相当合情合理：我断言我们在该群中已经看到了单位元（这显然在其中），并且能看到8 个固定单个顶点的 3 阶元素，
We haven't proved that yet, although it's pretty reasonable if you think about how it permutes the vertices and you think of what possible things we're getting in this group: I claim we already see in this group the identity element (we know the identity element), and we can see eight elements of order 3 fixing a single vertex,

146
00:37:31,436 --> 00:37:57,516
因为每个顶点对应 3 个元素，但其中一个是单位元，所以每个顶点给出2 个非平凡旋转，4 个顶点一共得到 8 个旋转。因此群中只剩下 3 个元素了，对吧？只剩下 3 个元素，因为它是 12 元群。
because each vertex gives you—there are three elements here, but one of them is the identity element, so you get these two non-trivial rotations, and you get 8 rotations that way. So there are only 3 elements left in the group, right? Three elements left because it's a 12-element group.

147
00:37:57,516 --> 00:38:01,577
而这几个元素阶数都是 2，事实上它们固定一条棱！
And those elements all have order 2, and in fact they fix an edge!

148
00:38:01,577 --> 00:38:16,829
这很有趣：你看，有 6 条棱，所以一条棱的稳定子群——如果该群在棱上传递作用（确实如此）——一条棱的稳定子群阶数为 2。
That's interesting: you see, there are 6 edges, so the stabilizer of an edge—if this group permutes the edges transitively, and it does—the stabilizer of an edge has order 2.

149
00:38:16,829 --> 00:38:24,902
那些实际上就是不同的……你们知道，共轭类。我稍后再讲共轭类。
And those are in fact the different... you know, the conjugacy class. Well, I'll do conjugacy classes later.

150
00:38:24,902 --> 00:38:39,560
如果你了解四个字母上的交错群 A_4，你不能包含形如(1 2) 这样的置换，不能包含那样的置换：那些 2 阶对换不在交错群中，因为它们是奇置换。
And if you know the alternating group on four letters, you can't have a permutation like (1 2) in it, you can't have a permutation like that: those elements of order 2 are not in the alternating group, because that's an odd permutation.

151
00:38:39,560 --> 00:38:48,014
但你可以有形如两个对换之积的 2 阶元素：例如 (1 2)(3 4)。
But you could have an element of order 2 that looks like this: the product of two transpositions.

152
00:38:48,014 --> 00:38:57,945
这正是这些2 阶元素对顶点的作用：即它对换这两个顶点，并对换另外两个顶点。
And that's in fact what these elements of order 2 do to the vertices: namely, it would switch these two vertices and it would switch these two vertices.

153
00:38:57,945 --> 00:39:12,549
我一时忘了在那时它固定哪条棱，对吧，这条棱，如果交换，就把四面体翻转过来。它把两条对棱都固定了！
And I forget what edge it stabilizes at that point—right, this edge here, if it switches, it turns the tetrahedron upside down. It fixes both!

154
00:39:12,549 --> 00:39:26,060
是的，你说得对，它两条都固定：如果它置换这两个顶点，并置换另外两个顶点，它就固定这条棱，并且恰好也固定对面的棱。那它是如何把四面体翻转过来的呢？
Yes, you're right, it fixes both: if it permutes these two vertices and it permutes these two vertices, it fixes this edge, and it also happens to have the property of fixing that edge. And how does it turn the tetrahedron upside down?

155
00:39:26,060 --> 00:39:31,860
没关系，这就是为什么我们需要模型。好的，留给你们思考。
Never mind, that's why we have models. Okay, I'll let you think about that.

156
00:39:31,860 --> 00:39:55,619
下一个正多面体——是的，A_4 是：它是S_4 中由偶置换构成的子群。它是 S_4 中满足将其视作置换矩阵时行列式为 1 而非 -1 的元素 g。
The next regular solid—yes, A_4 is: it's the subgroup of S_4 consisting of the even permutations. It's the elements g in S_4 such that when you view them as permutation matrices, the determinant of g is equal to 1, not -1.

157
00:39:55,619 --> 00:40:09,802
所以这是一个指数为 2 的子群。这个指数为 2 的子群正是旋转群。当我们转向下一个正多面体时：你看，四面体的特点是面都是三角形，并且每个顶点周围有3 个三角形，对吧？
So that's a subgroup of index 2. This subgroup of index 2 turns out to be Now when you go to the next regular solid: so you see, notice that this has the property that the faces are triangles, and we have three triangles around a point, right?

158
00:40:09,802 --> 00:40:16,863
如果你在每个点周围放 4 个三角形并将它闭合起来，就得到了所谓的正八面体（octahedron），因为它是八个面。
If you put four triangles around a point and you close it up, you get what's called the octahedron, because it has eight faces now.

159
00:40:16,863 --> 00:40:31,306
如果我们尝试确定它的旋转群：如果我们取穿过相对顶点的轴，我们现在就有了绕该轴的4 阶旋转。
And if we try to determine its rotation group: well, if we take an axis through the opposite vertices, we now have a rotation of order 4 around here.

160
00:40:31,306 --> 00:40:43,840
哎呀，这就是磁力片的毛病，真该死！我们再试一次。我就知道这行不通！好吧，也许能行，我们看看会发生什么。
Whoa, that's the problem with magnets, damn thing! Let's try again. I knew this would never work! Well, maybe it'll work, let's see what happens.

161
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:57,442
这里，一个……太棒了！要成了，要成了！我缺了什么？缺了一片，不过没关系，你们可以想象出来。
Here, one... marvelous! It's going to work, it's going to work! What am I missing? I'm missing a piece, but that's okay, you can imagine that.

162
00:40:57,442 --> 00:41:07,149
看，没关系。这就是物理学与数学的区别！
Look, never mind. This is the difference between physics and mathematics!

163
00:41:07,149 --> 00:41:23,909
以前我最讨厌我的物理实验课——我不知道你们做不做这些实验——我们会有实验去测万有引力常数之类的东西，我们会有那些无摩擦的物体滑来滑去、上下起落，我们要掐秒表或者测量闪光，诸如此类很酷的事情。
What I used to hate about my labs in physics—I don't know if you guys do these labs—we'd have a lab where we'd test the universal constant of gravitation, something like that, and we'd have these frictionless things sliding around and dropping up and down, and we'd be timing them or measuring flashes of light or all kinds of cool things.

164
00:41:23,909 --> 00:41:35,346
然后你回家，对吧，写实验报告，计算万有引力常数，结果差了7 个数量级！
And then you'd go home, right, and you'd write up your lab report, and you calculate the universal constant of gravitation, and it would be off by seven orders of magnitude!

165
00:41:35,346 --> 00:41:46,680
于是，因为你预先知道答案，你就从万有引力常数出发倒推你应该观察到的实验数据，然后这样就“证明”了！但这又太完美了，对吧？
So then, since you knew the answer, you'd start with the universal constant of gravitation and work backwards to what you should have observed, and then it would prove that! But that was too good, right?

166
00:41:46,680 --> 00:41:55,836
因为助教一眼就能看穿，所以你得稍微改动一点点，让它落在万有引力常数的一个数量级误差之内。
Because then the lab assistant would know, so then you'd have to fudge it a little bit so you'd get within one order of the universal constant of gravitation.

167
00:41:55,836 --> 00:42:09,602
好的，所以这里我们有：如果我们固定这个顶点，我们就有一个 4 阶旋转元素，并且对任意一对对顶都可以这样做旋转。这表明该群在顶点上传递作用。
Okay, so here we have: if we fix this vertex, we have an element of order 4, and we can do that for any pair of opposite vertices—a rotation. So that shows that it permutes the vertices transitively.

168
00:42:09,602 --> 00:42:22,317
一共有6 个顶点，任意顶点的稳定子群阶数为 4，所以该群的阶为 24（6 × 4）：6 个顶点，稳定子群为 4 阶。
There are 6 vertices, the stabilizer of any vertex has order 4, so the group has order 24 (6 × 4): 6 vertices, stabilizer of order 4.

169
00:42:22,317 --> 00:42:28,620
事实证明正八面体的对称群就是四个字母上的对称群 S_4。
That turns out to be the symmetric group on four letters, the symmetry group of the octahedron.

170
00:42:28,620 --> 00:42:40,910
这稍微有点难看出它置换的是哪四个对象，因为正如你们注意到的，有 6 个顶点、8 个面、12 条棱，对吧？
And it's a little hard to see which four things are being permuted, because as you notice, there are 6 vertices, and then there are 8 faces, and there are 12 edges, right?

171
00:42:40,910 --> 00:43:04,212
所以要寻找被置换的 4 个对象看起来有点奇怪，但我把它作为一道习题留给你们。（学生提问）什么？对。稳定子群——好的，我们指出这一点：在群作用中有时会出现这种情况。
So it looks a little weird to try to find four things that are being permuted, but I'll leave that to you as an exercise. Pardon? Yeah. Stabilizers—now, okay, let's point that out: that can sometimes happen in a group action.

172
00:43:04,212 --> 00:43:16,805
例如，这没有任何区别；我们只知道另一个顶点的稳定子群是一个共轭子群，但共轭有时保持该子群不变。
For example, it doesn't make any difference; all we know is that the stabilizer of another vertex is a conjugate subgroup, but conjugation sometimes preserves the subgroup.

173
00:43:16,805 --> 00:43:32,890
例如，如果我有一个群作用，G 作用在像 G/H 这样的集合上——假设这是我们的集合 S，假设 H 是正规子群（这是最极端的情形）——
So for example, if I had a group action, so G acts, as we saw, on anything like G/H—suppose this is our set S, suppose H is a normal subgroup, this is the most extreme case—

174
00:43:32,890 --> 00:43:50,356
那么对所有 s 都有 G_s = H，即完全相同的子群固定 S 中的每一个点。它是一个共轭子群，但对于正规子群而言，共轭并不改变它。
then G_s is equal to H for all s, namely the same subgroup stabilizes every point in S. It's a conjugate subgroup, but for a normal subgroup, you don't move.

175
00:43:50,356 --> 00:44:05,564
因此发生的情况是——奇妙之处在于——群中将这个顶点映到那个顶点的元素，将这个4 阶子群共轭变换到自身，这就是为什么这个顶点的稳定子群与那个顶点的稳定子群相同。
So what happens is—and that's what's amazing—the element in the group that takes this vertex to this vertex conjugates this subgroup of order 4 into itself, and that's why the stabilizer of this vertex is the same as the stabilizer of that vertex.

176
00:44:05,564 --> 00:44:17,737
但从计数公式的角度来看，一旦你验证了可以从任意顶点到达任意另一个顶点——第一个旋转群表明可以从这四个顶点中的任意一个到达任意另一个，然后如果我绕此处的轴旋转，
But from the point of view of the counting formula, once you verify that you can get from any vertex to any other—and the first rotation group shows that you get from any of these four vertices to any other, and then if I rotate from here around here,

177
00:44:17,737 --> 00:44:32,578
就可以从这个顶点到达那个顶点，再下到这一个，从而可以从 6 个顶点中的任意一个到达任意另一个——那么群的阶就是顶点数乘以顶点的稳定子群阶数（4）。所以这个群的阶是 24。
I can get from this vertex to this one, and then down to this one, so I can get from any of the 6 to any other—then the order of the group is the number of vertices times the stabilizer of the vertex, which is 4. So this group has order 24.

178
00:44:32,578 --> 00:44:53,774
好的，最后一种情形：正八面体，或者它的对偶多面体立方体，G 的阶是 24，事实上 G 同构于 S_4，虽然我还没有告诉大家它置换的是哪四个对象（正方体的 4 条空间对角线），
Okay, final case: so the octahedron, or its dual, the cube, the order of G is 24, and in fact G is isomorphic to S_4, although I haven't told you what four things it's permuting,

179
00:44:53,774 --> 00:45:02,266
因为这里我们还没像前一个情形那样给出一组自然的四个对象。最后的情形：你可以在一个顶点周围放 5 个正三角形。
because we haven't gotten a natural set of four things here like we did here. Final case: you can put five triangles around a vertex.

180
00:45:02,266 --> 00:45:10,330
如果你在一个顶点周围放 6 个正三角形，在平面上就铺平了；但在三维空间中，你仍然可以在一个顶点周围放 5 个三角形。
If you put six equilateral triangles around a vertex, you flatten out in the plane; but in space, you can still put five triangles around a vertex.

181
00:45:10,330 --> 00:45:22,995
我不知道我敢不敢尝试——你们觉得我可以试试吗？为什么不呢，我来试试看……这些磁力片吸力不太好，算了！
I don't know if I dare to try—you think I can try? Why not, I'm going to try... This magnet isn't going to work too well, forget it!

182
00:45:22,995 --> 00:45:32,613
如果在一个顶点周围放 5 个正三角形，就得到所谓的正二十面体（icosahedron）；它由 20 个面闭合而成，古希腊著名的几何形体。
If you put five triangles around a vertex, you get something called an icosahedron; it closes up with 20 faces, a famous Greek figure.

183
00:45:32,613 --> 00:46:08,940
四面体每个顶点周围有 3 个三角形；正八面体有 4 个三角形；如果你放 5 个三角形，就得到了正二十面体，它有——它有 20 个顶点和 12 个面，所有面都是五边形……对不起，是三角形，抱歉，我弄反了，是的！
So this has 3 triangles around a vertex; the octahedron has 4 triangles; and then if you put five triangles, you get the icosahedron, which has—which has 20 vertices and 12 faces, all of which are pentagons... I'm sorry, which are triangles, I'm sorry, I'm going the wrong way, yeah!

184
00:46:08,940 --> 00:46:19,240
它是 20 个面和 12 个顶点，谢谢！我刚才记成正十二面体了。谢谢，你说得对。
It's 20 faces and 12 vertices, thank you! I was thinking of the dodecahedron. Thank you, you're right.

185
00:46:19,240 --> 00:46:23,359
所以它有 20 个面、30 条棱。
So it has 20 faces, it has 30 edges.

186
00:46:23,359 --> 00:46:29,236
我得在书里找一张它的插图，下次我保证带来，因为我想多讲讲这个群。
I have to find a picture of this in a book, I'll bring it in next time, I promise, because I want to talk about this group more.

187
00:46:29,236 --> 00:46:53,091
同样地，SO(3) 中保持正二十面体的有限子群在顶点上传递作用；由于每个顶点连出 5 个面，绕每个顶点都有一个 5 阶旋转。这意味着该群的阶是 12 × 5，即 60。
Again, the finite subgroup of SO(3) that preserves the regular icosahedron permutes the vertices transitively; and since there are five triangles coming out of each vertex, you have a rotation of order 5 around each vertex. And that means that the order of the group is 12 × 5, which is 60.

188
00:46:53,091 --> 00:47:00,019
事实证明，该群本身就是五个字母上的交错群 A_5，虽然我暂时还无法告诉大家被置换的是哪五个对象。
And it turns out that the group itself is the alternating group on five letters, A_5, although again I can't tell you which five things are being per- muted.

189
00:47:00,019 --> 00:47:08,438
正如我所说，这是一个非常著名的群，因为它是第一个单群，是第一个没有非平凡正规子群的群。我们将证明这一点。
That's really, as I say, a very famous group, because it's the first simple group, it's the first group without normal subgroups. We're going to prove that.

190
00:47:08,438 --> 00:47:15,648
现在我可以告诉你们我一直答应要讲的关于宇宙形状的最新假说了。
And now I can tell you what I've been promising to tell you about the latest conjecture on the shape of the universe.

191
00:47:15,648 --> 00:47:25,084
好的，数学家提出了一个假说，大约在一个月内就会被天文学家推翻，但我现在还有机会讲一讲！
Okay, so there's a conjecture put out by mathematicians, which is going to be destroyed by the astronomers in about a month, but I still have a chance to talk about it!

192
00:47:25,084 --> 00:47:46,916
这个假说是：宇宙是一个闭合的三维流形空间，事实上宇宙是陪集空间 SO(3) 模去正二十面体的对称群，即一个陪集空间。
And it's that the universe is a closed shape which is a three-dimensional object, and in fact the universe is the coset space SO(3) modulo the symmetry group of an icosahedron, namely it's a coset space.

193
00:47:46,916 --> 00:47:52,520
现在大家必须理解 SO(3) 是一个三维空间。为什么 SO(3) 是一个三维空间呢？
Now you have to understand that SO(3) is a three-dimensional manifold. Why is SO(3) a three-dimensional manifold?

194
00:47:52,520 --> 00:48:10,321
因为 SO(3) 传递作用在二维球面 S^2 上，且单点的稳定子群同构于 SO(2)。
Well, because SO(3) acts transitively on the 2-sphere, with the stabilizer of a point isomorphic to SO(2).

195
00:48:10,321 --> 00:48:18,132
而 SO(2) 显然是一维群：它是绕一个角度的旋转，你有旋转角度的选择自由，那是一维群。
Now SO(2) is clearly a one-dimensional group: it's rotations by an angle, and you have a choice of the angle, that's a one-dimensional group.

196
00:48:18,132 --> 00:48:39,726
因此正如我们有计数公式（集合的阶等于群的阶除以稳定子群的阶），流形的维数等于群的维数减去稳定子群的维数：所以 2 + 1 得到一个三维群。因此这实际上是一个三维空间，是一个闭三维流形。
So just as we have the counting formula that the order of a set is the order of a group divided by the order of the stabilizer, the dimension of a space is the dimension of the group minus the dimension of the stabilizer: so 2 + 1 gives a three-dimensional group. So this in fact is a three-dimensional space, it's a closed three-dimensional manifold.

197
00:48:39,726 --> 00:48:51,682
如果你用一个有限群取陪集空间（商流形），你也会得到一个具有非常有趣的代数拓扑性质的闭三维空间：这被称为庞加莱三维球面（同调三维球）。
And if you take the coset space by a finite group, you also get a closed three-dimensional manifold with very interesting what's called algebraic topology: this is called the Poincaré 3-sphere.

198
00:48:51,682 --> 00:49:08,692
它之所以被称为庞加莱三维球面，在数学史上非常重要，因为庞加莱非常关心是否能判定一个在代数拓扑性质上与三维球面 S^3 相同的空间是否就是 S^3。
And the reason it was called the Poincaré 3-sphere, it was—it's very important in the history of mathematics because Poincaré was very interested in determining if something looks algebraically topologically like the 3-sphere.

199
00:49:08,692 --> 00:49:12,025
S^3 存在于四维空间中。
So here's the 3-sphere, it's in 4-space, of course.

200
00:49:12,025 --> 00:49:21,571
学过代数拓扑的同学知道，庞加莱在 20 世纪初发明了一种空间的拓扑不变量，称为同调群。
Those of you who have studied algebraic topology know that Poincaré at the beginning of this century invented some invariants of shapes called homology.

201
00:49:21,571 --> 00:49:34,450
三维球面的性质是：其零阶同调群H_0 是 Z，一阶同调群 H_1 是 0，二阶同调群 H_2 是 0，三阶同调群 H_3 是 Z。
And the 3-sphere has the property that its 0-th homology is Z, its first homology is 0, its second homology is 0, and its third homology group is Z.

202
00:49:34,450 --> 00:49:52,158
庞加莱证明了这个奇妙的空间具有与三维球面完全相同的同调群——完全相同的同调群。但它不具备相同的基本群（fundamental group），基本群是庞加莱定义的另一个不变量。
And Poincaré proved that this weird space had exactly the same homology as the 3-sphere—exactly the same homology as the 3-sphere. What it doesn't have is what's called the same fundamental group, which is another invariant that Poincaré defined.

203
00:49:52,158 --> 00:50:07,743
三维球面的基本群是平凡群，而这个奇妙的庞加莱同调三维球的基本群是一个比 A_5 稍大的群（二元二十面体群），它的阶是 120，商群为 A_5。
And the fundamental group here is trivial for the 3-sphere, and the fundamental group for this weird Poincaré 3-sphere is a group a little larger than A_5, which has order 120 and has quotient group A_5.

204
00:50:07,743 --> 00:50:20,377
这被称为\widetilde{A}_5，正是这一点使庞加莱能够将该空间与三维球面区分开来，因为尽管它的同调群相同，它却具有不同的拓扑不变量。
So that's called \widetilde{A}_5, and that allowed Poincaré to distinguish this space from the 3-sphere, because it had a different topological invariant even though its homology was the same.

205
00:50:20,377 --> 00:50:30,458
所以当你学代数拓扑时，这是一个著名的范例。现在为什么数学家要把这样一个著名的例子拉扯进宇宙的形状中呢？
So when you study algebraic topology, this is a famous example. Now why are mathematicians trying to drag some famous example into the shape of the universe?

206
00:50:30,458 --> 00:50:38,553
如果上帝真的用到了所有这些漂亮的范例，那当然很美妙！但天文学家现在正在检验宇宙微波背景辐射数据来验证。
Well, it would be nice—it would be nice if God used all these nice examples! But the astronomers are now testing out the background radiation data to see.

207
00:50:38,553 --> 00:50:46,926
这种假设预言了各种奇特现象，比如如果你仰望那一侧的天空，所看到的景象与你低头看另一侧天空看到的完全相同，诸如此类。
This prediction predicts all kinds of weird things, like if you look up at the sky over there, you see the same thing as if you look down at the sky down there, things like that.

208
00:50:46,926 --> 00:50:49,868
而我们至今并没有观测到这些现象。但至少这就是科学！
And we haven't seen those things. But at least that's science!

209
00:50:49,868 --> 00:51:00,865
科学就是，本世纪卡尔·波普尔（Karl Popper）对科学命题的一个伟大定义：它是可证伪的（falsifiable）——你永远无法彻底证实它，但你可以证伪它。
Science is, you know, one of the great definitions of a scientific proposition by Karl Popper this century was something that's falsifiable: you can never prove it, but you can prove it false.

210
00:51:00,865 --> 00:51:12,727
这就是科学陈述与文学陈述之间的区别。好的，所以这是一个假定宇宙作为一个三维流形具有这种形状的陈述。
That's the difference between a scientific statement and a statement about literature. Okay, so this is a statement that the universe has this shape as a three-dimensional object.

211
00:51:12,727 --> 00:51:16,280
因此现在我们可以检验并证伪它，然后再去寻找别的模型。
So now we can test it and prove it false, and then try to find something else.

212
00:51:16,280 --> 00:51:24,012
好的，下次我们将更多地探讨正二十面体。
Okay, so we'll do more about the icosahedron next time.
